From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 14:41:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] brand: user-facing brand + doc-link sweep (code)

Repoint user-facing documentation/help links from zed.dev to the fork
(docs -> https://iammaxim.github.io/zedium/docs, repo/menus ->
https://github.com/IamMaxim/zedium). The fork ships no docs site yet, so
these intentionally 404 until GitHub Pages is published.

- release_channel: app_id() dev.zed.Zed* -> dev.zedium.Zedium* (runtime
  Wayland/X11 WM_CLASS; must match the patch-0027 macOS bundle ids),
  app_identifier() Zed-Editor-* -> Zedium-Editor-*, docs base -> fork.
- zed_urls.rs: delete the dead account/start-trial/upgrade/terms/privacy/
  edit-prediction/skills helpers (sign-in + billing are gone); repoint the
  live rules/acp helpers to the fork and drop their unused cx/server_url.
- Delete the dead OpenAccountSettings action + handler.
- Remove the Zed-Pro upsell in the agent thread payment-required callout
  (now a provider-neutral "usage limit reached" message).
- Help menu: drop "Zed Twitter" / "Join the Team"; add "Zedium on GitHub".
- Repoint MCP OAuth CIMD_URL to the fork's client-metadata document.
- Neutralize zed.dev brand strings in ui component examples + a settings
  placeholder; repoint inherited doc-comment links.

Cloud-transport internals (http_client build_zed_*_url, the admin
impersonate call) and back-compat provider ids keep their zed.dev strings
and are handled via the verifier allowlist, not rebranded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
